        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How to increase authorised capital?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Verify AOA permits increase, hold Board Meeting, pass Ordinary Resolution at EGM, file Form SH-7 with ROC Haryana at Chandigarh within 30 days. Pay Haryana stamp duty (0.15% of increase) and ROC filing fee via MCA V3 portal. Patron handles the entire process for Gurugram companies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is Form SH-7?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Form SH-7 is the statutory form filed with the ROC to notify alteration in share capital under Section 61. It includes the e-MOA module for updating Clause V (Capital Clause), stamp duty payment, and attachments. Filed on MCA V3 portal with digital signature and CS/CA certification."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the stamp duty in Haryana?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Haryana charges 0.15% of the increase in authorised capital, subject to a maximum of Rs 25 lakh. Example: increasing by Rs 1 crore = Rs 15,000 stamp duty. Paid electronically via MCA portal during SH-7 filing. Auto-calculated based on registered office state."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What resolution is needed?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "An Ordinary Resolution (simple majority of voting shareholders) at an EGM is sufficient under Section 61(1)(a). Unless the AOA specifically requires a Special Resolution (rare), Ordinary Resolution is the standard requirement."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does the process take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "7-15 working days end-to-end from Board Meeting to MCA Master Data update. For closely-held companies with shareholder consent to shorter EGM notice, 7-10 days. ROC processing takes 5-7 working days after SH-7 submission."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the penalty for late filing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Under Section 450: Rs 10,000 initial penalty + Rs 1,000 per day of continuing default. Maximum Rs 2 lakh for the company and Rs 50,000 for the officer in default. Extended non-compliance may affect company ACTIVE status on MCA."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can authorised capital be decreased?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cancellation of unissued shares under Section 61(1)(e) reduces authorised capital without court approval. Reduction of paid-up capital requires NCLT approval under Section 66. Cancellation of unissued shares is filed via SH-7."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the cost of capital change?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Total cost includes ROC fee (Rs 5,000-75,000+ based on slab), Haryana stamp duty (0.15% of increase, max Rs 25 lakh), and professional fee (from Rs 3,999). Patron provides a transparent estimate before engagement. Quick Answers Authorised capital badhane ka process kya hai? Board Meeting -> EGM mein Ordinary Resolution -> 30 din mein Form SH-7 ROC Haryana mein file karo -> Stamp duty pay karo -> MCA Master Data update hota hai. Haryana mein stamp duty kitni lagti hai? Increase amount ka 0.15%, maximum Rs 25 lakh tak. MCA portal par electronically pay hota hai. Kitna time lagta hai? 7-15 working days. Startup ke liye fast-track 7-10 din mein ho jata hai."
