                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How to increase authorised capital?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Verify AOA permits increase, hold Board Meeting, pass Ordinary Resolution at EGM, file Form SH-7 with ROC Haryana at Chandigarh within 30 days. Pay Haryana stamp duty (0.15% of increase) and ROC filing fee via MCA V3 portal. Patron handles the entire process for Gurugram companies.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Form SH-7?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Form SH-7 is the statutory form filed with the ROC to notify alteration in share capital under Section 61. It includes the e-MOA module for updating Clause V (Capital Clause), stamp duty payment, and attachments. Filed on MCA V3 portal with digital signature and CS/CA certification.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the stamp duty in Haryana?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Haryana charges 0.15% of the increase in authorised capital, subject to a maximum of Rs 25 lakh. Example: increasing by Rs 1 crore = Rs 15,000 stamp duty. Paid electronically via MCA portal during SH-7 filing. Auto-calculated based on registered office state.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What resolution is needed?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>An Ordinary Resolution (simple majority of voting shareholders) at an EGM is sufficient under Section 61(1)(a). Unless the AOA specifically requires a Special Resolution (rare), Ordinary Resolution is the standard requirement.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does the process take?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>7-15 working days end-to-end from Board Meeting to MCA Master Data update. For closely-held companies with shareholder consent to shorter EGM notice, 7-10 days. ROC processing takes 5-7 working days after SH-7 submission.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for late filing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Under Section 450: Rs 10,000 initial penalty + Rs 1,000 per day of continuing default. Maximum Rs 2 lakh for the company and Rs 50,000 for the officer in default. Extended non-compliance may affect company ACTIVE status on MCA.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can authorised capital be decreased?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Cancellation of unissued shares under Section 61(1)(e) reduces authorised capital without court approval. Reduction of paid-up capital requires NCLT approval under Section 66. Cancellation of unissued shares is filed via SH-7.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the cost of capital change?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Total cost includes ROC fee (Rs 5,000-75,000+ based on slab), Haryana stamp duty (0.15% of increase, max Rs 25 lakh), and professional fee (from Rs 3,999). Patron provides a transparent estimate before engagement.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Authorised capital badhane ka process kya hai?</strong> Board Meeting -> EGM mein Ordinary Resolution -> 30 din mein Form SH-7 ROC Haryana mein file karo -> Stamp duty pay karo -> MCA Master Data update hota hai.</p><p><strong>Haryana mein stamp duty kitni lagti hai?</strong> Increase amount ka 0.15%, maximum Rs 25 lakh tak. MCA portal par electronically pay hota hai.</p><p><strong>Kitna time lagta hai?</strong> 7-15 working days. Startup ke liye fast-track 7-10 din mein ho jata hai.</p>

            </div>
